All six features are implemented and verified. Here's a summary of what changed:

**`app/auth.py`** — `require_api_key` now validates the `X-API-Key` header against `VALID_API_KEYS`; returns the username on success, raises HTTP 401 on missing/invalid key.

**`app/main.py`** — Four changes:
- **`GET /tasks`** — Added optional query params `status`, `priority`, `assigned_to` (combinable filters) plus `page` (default 1) and `page_size` (default 20) for pagination. Filtering happens before slicing.
- **`POST /tasks`** — Requires auth via `Depends(require_api_key)`. Validates `project_id` exists (404 if not), auto-generates a unique integer ID, appends to the in-memory list, returns 201.
- **`PUT /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Partial update using `TaskUpdate.model_dump(exclude_unset=True)` so only provided fields are changed. Returns 404 if task not found.
- **`DELETE /tasks/{task_id}`** — Requires auth. Returns 204 on success, 404 if task not found.

Smoke tests covering auth rejection, all filter combinations, pagination, create (including missing project), partial update, and delete all passed.
